wasn't voluntary.

493
00:23:53.182 --> 00:23:54.684
That it was forced on you.

494
00:23:57.979 --> 00:23:59.147
I'ma do you a favor

495
00:23:59.272 --> 00:24:00.773
and forget we had
this conversation.

496
00:24:00.940 --> 00:24:01.940
I'ma forget it.

497
00:24:02.024 --> 00:24:03.818
And I'ma go back inside

498
00:24:03.985 --> 00:24:05.194
to my retirement party

499
00:24:05.695 --> 00:24:09.991
and celebrate my thirty five
years of loyal service

500
00:24:10.116 --> 00:24:12.118
to this fuckin' city
and its people.

501
00:24:12.827 --> 00:24:14.245
I'm gon' do that.

502
00:24:14.704 --> 00:24:16.581
You gon' fuck
right the hell off.

503
00:24:16.706 --> 00:24:18.916
♪♪

504
00:24:30.553 --> 00:24:31.971
[music fades]

505
00:24:32.638 --> 00:24:34.015
[Breeze] Just give me a name...

506
00:24:35.099 --> 00:24:37.476
I can have our people
go even up the score.

507
00:24:38.144 --> 00:24:39.437
I'm good. man.

508
00:24:40.354 --> 00:24:41.564
This on me.

509
00:24:42.982 --> 00:24:45.109
Maybe you should lay low
for a minute. though.

510
00:24:45.276 --> 00:24:46.569
[groans]

511
00:24:46.736 --> 00:24:48.404
Crew see you like this...

512
00:24:49.614 --> 00:24:51.866
they might think
they sniffin' weakness.

513
00:24:52.491 --> 00:24:53.743
Might test you.

514
00:24:54.285 --> 00:24:56.120
I wish a nigga would.

515
00:24:58.164 --> 00:25:00.166
You ain't scared of nobody.

516
00:25:01.834 --> 00:25:03.461
Scared of me.

517
00:25:05.046 --> 00:25:06.589
My man.

518
00:25:10.259 --> 00:25:11.886
'Cause we had to burn
your other shit

519
00:25:12.011 --> 00:25:14.513
after the work we put in
at the boxing spot.

520
00:25:16.390 --> 00:25:17.950
It's gon' have niggas
hearin' you comin'

521
00:25:18.059 --> 00:25:19.810
from five blocks away.

522
00:25:22.605 --> 00:25:25.775
My moms tried to break me off
a new ride once.

523
00:25:26.859 --> 00:25:28.277
[dramatic music playing]

524
00:25:28.444 --> 00:25:29.904
Gave that shit back...

525
00:25:31.280 --> 00:25:33.115
'cause ain't nothin' free.

526
00:25:36.661 --> 00:25:38.246
Shit's yours.

527
00:25:39.705 --> 00:25:41.457
I don't need nothin'
back for it.

528
00:25:44.961 --> 00:25:46.879
I keep tellin' you we brothers.

529
00:25:49.257 --> 00:25:51.384
That might not mean
nothin' to you.

530
00:25:54.011 --> 00:25:56.555
That shit mean everything to me.

531
00:26:02.770 --> 00:26:04.355
Shit's dope as hell.

532
00:26:06.732 --> 00:26:08.276
Thanks. man.

533
00:26:10.194 --> 00:26:12.154
[music intensifies]

534
00:26:24.917 --> 00:26:26.127
[music fades]

535
00:26:30.256 --> 00:26:31.257
Ms. Thomas.

536
00:26:31.632 --> 00:26:32.967
Come on in.

537
00:26:40.683 --> 00:26:42.893
[birds chirping]

538
00:26:50.109 --> 00:26:51.444
Since you...

539
00:26:52.486 --> 00:26:54.238
was on the wagon
when you left...

540
00:26:56.240 --> 00:26:58.326
don't feel right to pour out
no liquor.

541
00:27:00.119 --> 00:27:01.412
[laughs softly]

542
00:27:02.580 --> 00:27:04.498
But I brought some
for you anyway.

543
00:27:06.500 --> 00:27:07.960
Do what you want with it.

544
00:27:14.550 --> 00:27:16.594
Don't know what to say
about your nephew.

545
00:27:17.678 --> 00:27:19.680
Can't even wrap
my head around that shit.

546
00:27:20.931 --> 00:27:22.308
Never will.

547
00:27:24.101 --> 00:27:26.270
But I'm all fucked up
out here. Lou-Lou.

548
00:27:29.148 --> 00:27:30.524
[inhales deeply]

549
00:27:30.691 --> 00:27:32.318
Don't even know what I'm doin'.

550
00:27:34.362 --> 00:27:35.946
Never been like this before.

551
00:27:36.822 --> 00:27:38.574
Don't have no feel for the game.

552
00:27:39.492 --> 00:27:41.160
[inhales deeply]

553
00:27:41.869 --> 00:27:43.746
I keep askin' myself
questions...

554
00:27:45.581 --> 00:27:46.957
but I ain't got no answers.

555
00:27:49.585 --> 00:27:51.295
[sighs] I wanna do right by you.

556
00:27:53.255 --> 00:27:54.340
Thing is...

557
00:27:54.965 --> 00:27:56.467
I don't know
what that look like.

558
00:27:57.176 --> 00:27:58.469
But I gotta do somethin'.

559
00:27:58.636 --> 00:28:00.221
[somber music playing]

560
00:28:00.388 --> 00:28:01.847
I gotta feel somethin'.

561
00:28:04.433 --> 00:28:05.643
Fuck.

562
00:28:07.103 --> 00:28:08.562
I miss you. Lou.

563
00:28:10.981 --> 00:28:12.191
[exhales softly]

564
00:28:13.442 --> 00:28:15.694
[inhales deeply. sighs]

565
00:28:21.409 --> 00:28:22.451
[music fades]

566
00:28:22.618 --> 00:28:23.702
Appreciate you seein' me.

567
00:28:24.328 --> 00:28:25.955
I was surprised
to hear from you.

568
00:28:26.455 --> 00:28:27.540
The last time we met.

569
00:28:27.706 --> 00:28:29.667
when Lou was at
the rehabilitation facility.

570
00:28:29.834 --> 00:28:32.002
you seemed skeptical of...

571
00:28:32.169 --> 00:28:34.130
psychiatry. generally. and...

572
00:28:34.296 --> 00:28:36.507
distrustful of me. specifically.

573
00:28:37.591 --> 00:28:38.968
Never said I ain't trust you.

574
00:28:39.093 --> 00:28:41.429
Just wasn't sold on what
you was sayin' about Lou.

575
00:28:41.762 --> 00:28:42.430
Hmm.

576
00:28:42.596 --> 00:28:44.348
And what I said about you
as well.

577
00:28:45.266 --> 00:28:47.560
If memory serves. I made
a remark about your anger

578
00:28:47.726 --> 00:28:48.894
that you didn't appreciate.

579
00:28:49.061 --> 00:28:50.622
You was talkin' about me
when I was payin' you

580
00:28:50.646 --> 00:28:51.646
to talk about my brother.

581
00:28:52.398 --> 00:28:55.151
And who are you paying me to
talk about today. Ms. Thomas?

582
00:28:57.153 --> 00:28:58.797
I was wondering if Lou said
anything about me

583
00:28:58.821 --> 00:28:59.947
you think I should know.

584
00:29:00.072 --> 00:29:01.240
[Dr. Caldwell] <i>I see.</i>

585
00:29:01.365 --> 00:29:03.051
My conversations with
your brother were confidential

586
00:29:03.075 --> 00:29:05.786
at the time that we had them
and they remain so.

587
00:29:05.953 --> 00:29:07.288
<i>even after his passing.</i>

588
00:29:07.830 --> 00:29:09.457
You shared stuff he said before.

589
00:29:09.623 --> 00:29:12.501
I shared what your brother
allowed me to share.

590
00:29:12.668 --> 00:29:13.752
Lou gone.

591
00:29:13.919 --> 00:29:16.213
What harm it gonna do to tell me
some of what he said?

592
00:29:17.798 --> 00:29:19.884
What are you hoping
to hear. Ms. Thomas?

593
00:29:21.177 --> 00:29:24.472
What is it you'd like
Lou to have said about you?

594
00:29:29.268 --> 00:29:30.311
I don't know.

595
00:29:32.438 --> 00:29:33.898
Just tryin' to remember him.

596
00:29:35.149 --> 00:29:36.233
That's all.

597
00:29:36.859 --> 00:29:38.299
It may be that whatever
you're hoping

598
00:29:38.444 --> 00:29:39.820
<i>your brother said about you</i>

599
00:29:39.987 --> 00:29:42.198
<i>is less about what he thought
about you...</i>

600
00:29:43.032 --> 00:29:45.618
but more so what you think
of yourself.

601
00:29:46.869 --> 00:29:49.538
[somber music playing]

602
00:29:49.705 --> 00:29:52.208
You makin' this shit about me
just like you did before.

603
00:29:52.791 --> 00:29:54.418
When you're in this office.

604
00:29:54.585 --> 00:29:55.585
on that couch.

605
00:29:55.711 --> 00:29:57.588
it is about you. Ms. Thomas.

606
00:29:58.923 --> 00:30:00.591
<i>It's always about you.</i>

607
00:30:05.346 --> 00:30:06.764
[music fades]

608
00:30:11.143 --> 00:30:12.311
[engine shuts off]

609
00:30:18.859 --> 00:30:19.859
[Baptiste] <i>Garcia!</i>

610
00:30:20.653 --> 00:30:23.572
<i>You fucked up my party
last night. you motherfucker.</i>

611
00:30:23.739 --> 00:30:25.157
[ominous music playing]

612
00:30:25.324 --> 00:30:27.243
Now I'ma fuck up yours.

613
00:30:30.454 --> 00:30:32.998
I'm just sayin'. shit's ill.
That's all.

614
00:30:33.165 --> 00:30:34.165
[music fades]

615
00:30:34.250 --> 00:30:35.709
Can't get caught slippin'.

616
00:30:37.753 --> 00:30:38.796
[groans]

617
00:30:38.963 --> 00:30:40.714
Fuck y'all doin' here?

618
00:30:42.132 --> 00:30:44.885
Y'all need to be out there
servin' up this work.

619
00:30:45.844 --> 00:30:48.305
[Krank] Niggas shook about
what happened at the crib.

620
00:30:48.472 --> 00:30:50.891
Saw they life flash
in front of 'em and shit.

621
00:30:54.436 --> 00:30:55.896
So you stop workin'?

622
00:30:56.188 --> 00:30:57.481
We ain't been seein' you.

623
00:30:58.440 --> 00:31:01.652
And now it look like that 'cause
you got a little fucked up.

624
00:31:02.695 --> 00:31:04.947
Sometime a nigga
gotta take a minute.

625
00:31:06.532 --> 00:31:08.367
Fuck you just say to me?

626
00:31:08.492 --> 00:31:10.035
<i>I- I-I'm just sayin'.</i>

627
00:31:10.369 --> 00:31:14.206
sometime... you gotta
take a step back

628
00:31:14.373 --> 00:31:15.833
and reassess.

629
00:31:16.208 --> 00:31:17.626
<i>Get your life in order.</i>

630
00:31:17.793 --> 00:31:19.503
Shit's scary out here.

631
00:31:19.628 --> 00:31:20.628
Whoa.

632
00:31:20.754 --> 00:31:21.755
-Damn!
-Oh. fuck!

633
00:31:21.922 --> 00:31:23.465
<i>-Whoa!
-What the hell?!</i>

634
00:31:23.632 --> 00:31:24.842
Man. what the fuck?

635
00:31:24.967 --> 00:31:27.177
[Kanan] <i>Anybody else scared?</i>

636
00:31:27.344 --> 00:31:29.263
[dramatic music playing]

637
00:31:29.430 --> 00:31:32.433
'Cause I can't have
no scared niggas around me.

638
00:31:33.309 --> 00:31:36.687
You scared.
we gon' get you unscared.

639
00:31:36.854 --> 00:31:38.981
You shook.
we gon' get you unshook.

640
00:31:40.566 --> 00:31:42.192
Get the fuck back to work!

641
00:31:42.318 --> 00:31:43.444
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

642
00:31:43.611 --> 00:31:46.447
[indistinct chatter]

643
00:31:50.951 --> 00:31:53.370
[Baptiste] You know
how this shit works. Garcia.

644
00:31:54.371 --> 00:31:56.624
You only as good
as your clearance rate.

645
00:31:57.833 --> 00:32:00.461
But shoe leather doesn't always
get the job done.

646
00:32:00.628 --> 00:32:02.379
Sometimes we have to wade

647
00:32:02.546 --> 00:32:05.549
into the very shit
that we tryin' to clean up.

648
00:32:07.593 --> 00:32:09.261
But that shit can stick to you.

649
00:32:10.346 --> 00:32:12.056
Can't always clean it off.

650
00:32:17.895 --> 00:32:20.314
Who were you talkin' to
about Shawn Figueroa?

651
00:32:21.732 --> 00:32:24.777
There's a quid pro quo
to this work.

652
00:32:25.736 --> 00:32:28.155
To get information.
you have to give information.

653
00:32:28.572 --> 00:32:30.366
And that's the choice
you have to make:

654
00:32:30.532 --> 00:32:33.577
"What do I know that feels
safe enough to share?"

655
00:32:34.787 --> 00:32:36.455
And that Figueroa kid felt safe.

656
00:32:37.456 --> 00:32:41.752
He dropped a stick-up kid
the whole neighborhood hated.

657
00:32:42.795 --> 00:32:45.881
It felt like the safest
of the safe shit.

658
00:32:50.844 --> 00:32:51.970
I didn't know...

659
00:32:52.680 --> 00:32:54.348
they were gonna have him killed.

660
00:32:55.933 --> 00:32:57.935
And if they used police...

661
00:32:58.102 --> 00:32:59.353
they weren't from our precinct.

662
00:32:59.520 --> 00:33:00.562
Who made the call?

663
00:33:00.729 --> 00:33:02.231
Oh. some old-time gangsters.

664
00:33:02.398 --> 00:33:03.774
Barely even in the game anymore.

665
00:33:03.941 --> 00:33:05.234
I need a name.

666
00:33:05.859 --> 00:33:06.859
Shoo...

667
00:33:12.199 --> 00:33:14.451
Ishmael and Stephanie Henry.

668
00:33:15.661 --> 00:33:16.662
Snaps and Pop.

669
00:33:16.829 --> 00:33:19.623
[tense. ominous music playing]

670
00:33:19.748 --> 00:33:21.375
[sighs]

671
00:33:21.542 --> 00:33:22.668
Man. you got to believe me.

672
00:33:22.835 --> 00:33:25.796
I had no idea they was gonna
do that kid like that.

673
00:33:26.964 --> 00:33:29.633
And even now. I can't be
so certain that they did.

674
00:33:31.218 --> 00:33:35.764
They just had such a...
hard-on for that Raquel Thomas.

675
00:33:37.182 --> 00:33:39.768
Anything that tracked to her

676
00:33:39.935 --> 00:33:41.353
was something
they wanted to know.

677
00:33:42.229 --> 00:33:44.398
And I knew that
the Figueroa kid was...

678
00:33:44.815 --> 00:33:46.942
friends with Raquel Thomas' son.

679
00:33:49.194 --> 00:33:50.028
So I threw 'em a bone.

680
00:33:50.195 --> 00:33:52.114
[music intensifies]

681
00:33:52.823 --> 00:33:55.117
I had no idea

682
00:33:55.284 --> 00:33:57.244
it would end up how it did.

683
00:33:59.371 --> 00:34:00.371
[inhales sharply]

684
00:34:00.497 --> 00:34:02.166
The feds are all over this.

685
00:34:03.876 --> 00:34:05.919
-They're all over you.
-[Baptiste] <i>I know.</i>

686
00:34:06.336 --> 00:34:07.336
I know.

687
00:34:09.256 --> 00:34:12.217
And it's far bigger
than Figueroa.

688
00:34:14.928 --> 00:34:16.180
It's Howard.

689
00:34:17.639 --> 00:34:20.309
It's Burke. It's the whole...

690
00:34:20.684 --> 00:34:22.186
<i>fuckin' ball of wax.</i>

691
00:34:24.688 --> 00:34:26.231
<i>You're about the only...</i>

692
00:34:27.107 --> 00:34:29.818
<i>clean cop in the 117. Garcia.</i>

693
00:34:33.155 --> 00:34:34.656
Take a fucking bow.

694
00:34:36.408 --> 00:34:39.286
[music intensifies]

695
00:34:50.297 --> 00:34:52.341
[music fades]

696
00:34:53.634 --> 00:34:55.636
[Flossie] They say that.
over time.

697
00:34:55.803 --> 00:34:57.846
losing someone you love
gets easier.

698
00:34:58.013 --> 00:35:00.349
but... that's horseshit.

699
00:35:02.559 --> 00:35:03.727
Time's only made me sadder.

700
00:35:03.894 --> 00:35:06.063
It's made me miss Shira
even more.

701
00:35:06.230 --> 00:35:07.648
So. fuck time

702
00:35:07.815 --> 00:35:10.275
and fuck all the people
that say it gets easier.

703
00:35:15.489 --> 00:35:16.573
You feel better

704
00:35:17.241 --> 00:35:19.361
after you took out the nigga
who killed your daughter?

705
00:35:20.661 --> 00:35:22.371
[sighs]

706
00:35:24.164 --> 00:35:25.499
I didn't.

707
00:35:26.750 --> 00:35:28.043
And I don't regret what I did.

708
00:35:28.210 --> 00:35:30.170
but I don't feel any better.

709
00:35:30.337 --> 00:35:32.089
I don't miss my daughter
any less.

710
00:35:32.548 --> 00:35:33.548
But you got even.

711
00:35:34.216 --> 00:35:36.760
-Even's good.
-Even's gornisht. Marvin.

712
00:35:36.927 --> 00:35:39.263
Even is worse than losing.
It's nothing.

713
00:35:39.429 --> 00:35:41.014
It's nowhere. It's purgatory.

714
00:35:41.181 --> 00:35:44.226
We're not here playing for even.
We're playing to win.

715
00:35:45.769 --> 00:35:47.539
Look. what do I know?
I'm just some Jewish broad

716
00:35:47.563 --> 00:35:50.357
from the Upper East Side.
but if you ask me.

717
00:35:50.524 --> 00:35:52.276
your best and only chance

718
00:35:52.442 --> 00:35:54.486
at winning this thing
is your daughter.

719
00:35:55.445 --> 00:35:56.864
Go all in on her. Marvin.

720
00:35:57.030 --> 00:35:59.741
She's your pocket aces
and your silver bullet.

721
00:36:00.158 --> 00:36:02.494
Bet the fucking house on her.

722
00:36:02.661 --> 00:36:05.205
[solemn music playing]

723
00:36:05.330 --> 00:36:06.540
I get it.

724
00:36:07.541 --> 00:36:09.126
I know you do.

725
00:36:10.586 --> 00:36:12.170
L'chaim. Marvin.

726
00:36:13.171 --> 00:36:14.506
L'chaim.

727
00:36:16.884 --> 00:36:18.093
[music fades]

728
00:36:18.260 --> 00:36:20.679
No one did more
to protect Raq than me.

729
00:36:21.346 --> 00:36:23.557
I mean. fixin' all the shit
she broke.

730
00:36:23.724 --> 00:36:25.767
buildin' back
the bridges she burned.

731
00:36:25.934 --> 00:36:27.254
But you-you-you can't
help someone

732
00:36:27.311 --> 00:36:29.271
that doesn't wanna help
themselves.

733
00:36:29.396 --> 00:36:30.916
And when they're drowning.
like she is.

734
00:36:31.023 --> 00:36:33.442
you gotta get as far away
as you can...

735
00:36:34.151 --> 00:36:35.944
or she'll drag you under
with her.

736
00:36:36.612 --> 00:36:37.613
[sighs]

737
00:36:38.280 --> 00:36:41.283
[gentle traditional music
playing in shop]

738
00:36:41.450 --> 00:36:43.619
She has not been
a reliable partner.

739
00:36:43.785 --> 00:36:45.871
She guaranteed me
a specific volume of demand

740
00:36:46.038 --> 00:36:47.038
that she has not met.

741
00:36:47.164 --> 00:36:49.291
Well. my young friend here.

742
00:36:49.458 --> 00:36:52.920
he can meet and surpass
those demands. Hafiz.

743
00:36:53.086 --> 00:36:54.922
And you won't get
all the bullshit

744
00:36:55.088 --> 00:36:56.340
that comes along with Raq.

745
00:36:56.465 --> 00:36:59.384
We movin' so much work right now
we can't keep up.

746
00:37:00.385 --> 00:37:02.179
What about
your current supplier?

747
00:37:02.554 --> 00:37:03.555
Well...

748
00:37:04.306 --> 00:37:05.849
We got enough room
for everybody.

749
00:37:06.683 --> 00:37:08.202
<i>And we gon' give you
a five percent bump</i>

750
00:37:08.226 --> 00:37:10.020
on what Raq has been payin'.

751
00:37:14.232 --> 00:37:15.984
Your friends in Manhattan

